    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0004545 .

obo:FLOPO_0986063 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "syconium ostiole"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the opening at the apex of the urn-shaped inflorescence receptacle of a fig (syconium), closed by overlapping ostiolar bracts."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:syconium_ostiole (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Mostly Ficus (bilabiate, prominent, sunken, closed ostiole), which is large and diagnostic: 328 statements in 9 floras, and PO has no class. Propose to PO, ideally together with a syconium inflorescence class. Not the stomatal or fungal ostiole. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "fig ostiole"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "orifice"@en,
        "ostiole"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030121 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986064 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "endostome"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the inner circle of segments of a double peristome (PO:0030042), usually a basal membrane bearing segments and cilia, inside the exostome."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:endostome (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Moss term used throughout bryophyte floras (306 statements, 4 floras) with its own colour, papillae and reduction. PO has only peristome and peristome tooth. Propose to PO (Bryophytes subset) together with exostome. Not the ovule endostome (opening of the inner integument), which the examples do not fit. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "endostomium"@en,
        "inner peristome"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030042 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986065 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pinna rachis"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A stalk (PO:0025066) that is the axis of a pinna of a bipinnate or more highly compound leaf, bearing the pinnules or pinna segments."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:pinna_rachis (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Bipinnate leaves (Acacia, many legumes; also Leea and ferns). PO leaf rachis (PO_0020055) is defined as the main axis only, so it cannot be used. Propose to PO together with pinna and pinnule. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "pinna axis"@en,
        "pinna rhachis"@en,
        "rachis of pinna"@en,
