        "rachis secondaire"@en,
        "secondary rachis"@en,
        "secondary rhachis"@en,
        "axe de la pinne"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0985027 ],
        obo:PO_0025066 .

obo:FLOPO_0986066 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "sporocarp"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A hard, bean- or nut-like structure of the heterosporous water ferns (Marsileaceae, Salviniaceae), derived from a modified leaf segment, that encloses the sori (PO:0025359) and their sporangia."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:sporocarp (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real, diagnostic structure (Marsilea, Pilularia, Azolla, Salvinia) with no PO class. The examples (hairy, sulcate, underground or below stem level, ovate in lateral view) are Marsilea sporocarps. 274 statements in 8 floras. Not the fungal fruit body. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "sporocarpe"@en,
        "sporocarps"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009026 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986067 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "corolla plica"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) of a sympetalous corolla (PO:0009059) that is a folded, often toothed or lobed extension of the corolla tube between two adjacent corolla lobes, as in Gentiana."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:corolla_plica (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: The qualities (broadly triangular, oblique, erose summit, entire) are those of Gentiana plicae, a standard character in Gentianaceae treatments of several floras. Propose to PO. Leaf plications of mosses are a quality (plicate), not this class. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "corolla fold"@en,
        "corolla plicae"@en,
        "sinus appendage"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "plica"@en,
        "plicae"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009059 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986068 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lithocyst"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An idioblast (PO:0000283) that contains a cystolith, a concretion of calcium carbonate on a cellulose stalk, visible on the surface of leaves and stems as a pale dot or short line."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:lithocyst (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real, diagnostic structure (Acanthaceae, Urticaceae, Moraceae, Cannabaceae) with no PO class; together with 'cystolith' it covers about 24 flora sources and 377 statements. The cystolith itself is a mineral body inside the cell. Floras describe what is seen, the cystolith-bearing cell, so the class is a kind of idioblast. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "cystolith"@en,
        "cystolithe"@en,
        "cystoliths"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0000283 .

obo:FLOPO_0986069 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "perispore"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure (PO:0009011) that is the outermost layer of the wall of a plant spore (PO:0025017), laid down outside the exospore from tapetal material, often folded, winged, reticulate or spiny, as in many ferns."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:perispore (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A key fern character (236 statements, 4 floras) with no class. PO moved the spore and pollen wall layers (exine etc.) to GO, which has spore wall GO:0031160 but no perine. Make it a FLOPO class and request it from GO, not PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "perisporium"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "perine"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025017 ],
        obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986070 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "perigynium beak"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the narrowed, prolonged distal portion of a perigynium (PO:0009044), above the body that encloses the achene, often bidentate at its orifice, as in Carex."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:perigynium_beak (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Carex key character (208 statements, 4 floras) measured and described apart from the perigynium body, and with its own tip ('beak pale brown at tip'), so 'apex part of perigynium' would merge it with the perigynium apex. Propose to PO, which already holds perigynium from FNA. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "beak of perigynium"@en,
        "perigynium rostrum"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009044 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986071 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pseudoparaphyllium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A small leaf-like, scale-like or filamentous outgrowth of a moss gametophore axis that is found only around a branch primordium or at the base of a branch, not scattered between the leaves."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:pseudoparaphyllium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Pleurocarpous moss character used in 4 floras (foliose/filamentous/lanceolate/absent). It differs from paraphyllium (PO_0030069), which grows between the leaves along the stem, so it is not a synonym. Propose upstream to PO next to paraphyllium. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "pseudo-paraphyllia"@en,
        "pseudo-paraphyllium"@en,
        "pseudoparaphyll"@en,
        "pseudoparaphyllia"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030020 ],
        obo:PO_0005679 .

obo:FLOPO_0986072 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "stelidium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is one of a usually paired tooth- or arm-like projection at the apex or sides of the gynostemium (FLOPO:0986015) of an orchid flower, flanking the anther, as in Bulbophyllum and Pleurothallidinae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:stelidium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real orchid structure with no class. Floras use it with shape, size and visibility (5 floras, 151 statements). It cannot be expressed as a region of the gynostemium. Propose it to PO together with gynostemium. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "column arm"@en,
        "column tooth"@en,
        "stelidia"@en,
