        "anther tail"@en,
        "connective appendages"@en,
        "connective appendix"@en,
        "appendice de l'anthère"@fr,
        "appendice du connectif"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009068 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986074 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "rhizophore"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A leafless, usually unbranched axis that arises at a branching point of the stem in Selaginella and grows towards the substrate, where it produces roots at its tip."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:rhizophore (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A distinct organ of Selaginella (spikemosses), described in five floras with length, diameter, hairiness and colour. PO has no class for it. Scientists still argue whether it is a root or a shoot, so the neutral parent 'plant axis' is the safe choice. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "rhizophores"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0025004 .

obo:FLOPO_0986075 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "limbidium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A leaf margin (PO:0020128) of a non-vascular leaf that is a border of elongate, often thick-walled cells that differ clearly from the cells of the lamina."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:limbidium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Moss leaf border (Fissidens and others). Mapping it to plain leaf margin would make 'limbidium absent' read as 'margin absent', so a subclass is needed. Propose to PO (Bryophytes subset). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "border of elongate cells"@en,
        "leaf border"@en,
        "limbidia"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0020128 .

obo:FLOPO_0986076 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "stipule lobe"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A free lobe, segment or fimbria of a divided stipule (PO:0020041)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:stipule_lobe (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Divided and fimbriate stipules are diagnostic (Rubiaceae, Euphorbiaceae, Rosaceae), and floras describe both the number and the shape of the lobes (triangular, lanceolate, linear to filiform). The lobe counts could come from flora_counted_parts ('-fid/-partite' gives a lobe count), but the shapes need a class. A stipule is not a phyllome, so phyllome lamina lobe (PO_0025514) does not apply. This follows the FLOPO 'X lobe' classes (calyx lobe FLOPO_0986005, corona lobe FLOPO_0986035). 115 statements here plus 40 under 'stipule segment'. Could be proposed to PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "lobe of stipule"@en,
        "stipular lobe"@en,
        "stipule lobes"@en,
        "stipule segment"@en,
        "stipule segments"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0020041 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986077 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hyaline cell"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A native plant cell (PO:0025606) of the leaf of Sphagnum that is large, dead and empty at maturity, often strengthened by fibrils and perforated by pores, and that holds water. Hyaline cells alternate with narrow living chlorophyllose cells in a network."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:hyaline_cell (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A distinct cell type used in every Sphagnum description (rhombic, fibrillose, pores counted). PO has other bryophyte cell types (alar cell, hydroid) but not this one. Propose to PO (Bryophytes subset). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "hyaline cells"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "hyalocyst"@en,
        "leucocyst"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0025606 .

obo:FLOPO_0986078 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "spine shield"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a hard, horny pad on the angle of the stem of a succulent Euphorbia, bearing the spines of a node, and that may be separate or run together with neighbouring pads into a continuous horny margin."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:spine_shield (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Standard character in the Kew African floras for spiny Euphorbia (Flora of Tropical East Africa, Flora Zambesiaca; 107 statements, about 70 taxa). PO has no class. Could be proposed to PO, though only for one genus group. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "spine shields"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009047 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986079 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "style head"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the thickened, often lobed or fusiform apical portion of a style (PO:0009074), bearing the receptive stigmatic surface and in Apocynaceae united with the anthers to form the gynostegium."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:style_head (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A distinct structure of Apocynaceae (81 statements in 3 floras). FLOPO's gynostegium (FLOPO_0986051) is already defined through the 'stigma head', which has no class. 'Style apex' would lose the structure. Propose it to PO upstream with the gynostegium question (issue 6). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "pistil head"@en,
        "stigma head"@en,
        "stylar head"@en,
        "stylehead"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "clavuncle"@en,
        "clavuncula"@en,
        "massue"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009074 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986080 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pseudostaminode"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A lobe or appendage of the staminal cup that stands between the filaments and does not derive from a stamen, as in many Amaranthaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:pseudostaminode (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Used in Amaranthaceae (Achyranthes, Tidestromia, Alternanthera) for outgrowths of the filament tube between the stamens. They are not staminodes, so the staminode class (PO_0009077) would be wrong. Diagnostic across 12 floras. Could be proposed to PO, with part_of the staminal tube (FLOPO_0986013) where that applies. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "interstaminal appendage"@en,
        "pseudo-staminode"@en,
        "pseudostaminodes"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009061 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986081 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "column foot"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A forward extension of the base of the column (gynostemium) of an orchid flower, to which the lateral sepals and the lip are often attached, together forming a mentum."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:column_foot (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure in many orchids (Dendrobium, Bulbophyllum, Eria) with its own length, curvature and free part, in five floras. It is an extension rather than just the base of the column, so 'base' would not fit. It sits next to the existing FLOPO classes mentum and gynostemium, so keep it in FLOPO with those orchid classes. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "foot of the column"@en,
        "gynostemium foot"@en,
        "pied de la colonne"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0986015 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986082 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "infrastaminal scale"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a thin, often fringed scale-like appendage on the inner face of the corolla tube, below the insertion of a stamen."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:infrastaminal_scale (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Key character in every Cuscuta description (FNA, other floras; 84 statements). It sits inside the tube below the stamens, not at the throat, so it is not corolline corona (FLOPO_0985021). Keep it local to FLOPO; low priority for PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "corolla scale"@en,
        "infrastaminal scales"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0985018 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986083 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "loment segment"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is one of the one-seeded segments into which a loment fruit (PO:0030101) is divided by constrictions and at which it breaks apart."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:loment_segment (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Counted and described in many legume genera (Aeschynomene, Humularia, Desmodium, Alysicarpus). Plain 'article' was rejected for lacking its organ; here the organ is clear. Propose to PO next to loment fruit. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "fruit article"@en,
        "fruit segment"@en,
        "joint of the pod"@en,
        "loment article"@en,
        "pod article"@en,
        "pod segment"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "article"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030101 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986084 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "bladder trap"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a small, hollow, stalked bladder developed from a leaf or leaf segment, with a mouth closed by a trapdoor and glandular trigger hairs, which catches small aquatic animals by suction (as in Utricularia)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:bladder_trap (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure without a class, used in 6 floras with 76 statements (globose or ovoid, stalked, glandular). Pitchers are already PO synonyms of vascular leaf, so this class covers only suction traps. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "bladder"@en,
        "trap"@en,
        "traps"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0006001 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986085 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "buttress root"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A root (PO:0009005) that grows strongly in thickness on its upper side near the base of the trunk, forming a flattened, plank-like ridge that joins the trunk to the ground."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:buttress_root (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: PO has prop (stilt) roots but no buttress. The quality buttressed (FLOPO:0991138) covers only presence ('with small buttresses'). Height, width, thickness and shape need a bearer: 69 statements in 6 floras. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "buttress"@en,
        "plank buttress"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "buttresses"@en,
        "contrefort"@en,
        "contreforts"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0000003 ],
        obo:PO_0009005 .

obo:FLOPO_0986086 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "perichaetium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure (PO:0009011) that is the group of modified leaves (perichaetal bracts) together with the archegonia they surround, at the female sex organ site of a moss or liverwort gametophyte."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:perichaetium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: PO has perichaetal bract (PO_0030030) but not the whole cluster. Floras describe the cluster as terminal or lateral, small, numerous or convolute, and count setae per perichaetium. Propose to PO upstream next to perichaetal bract. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "perichaetia"@en,
        "périchèse"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030018 ],
        obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986087 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "phyllopodium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part that is a short, persistent, stalk-like projection at the base of a fern leaf, to which the stipe is articulated and which remains after the leaf falls."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:phyllopodium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A standard term in fern floras (Polypodiaceae, grammitids, Elaphoglossum) with no PO class. Propose to PO upstream; PO will need to settle whether it is part of the leaf or the rhizome. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "phyllopod"@en,
        "phyllopodia"@en,
        "phyllopods"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986088 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "supra-alar cell"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A native plant cell (PO:0025606) located at the base of a non-vascular leaf (PO:0025075) just above the alar cells (PO:0030057), along the leaf margin."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:supra_alar_cell (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A named cell group of the moss leaf base, used in several moss floras with its own states (quadrate, rectangular, differentiated or not). It is the counterpart of the PO class alar cell PO:0030057 (subset Bryophytes). Propose to PO next to alar cell. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "supra-alar cells"@en,
        "supra-alar region cell"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0025606 .

obo:FLOPO_0986089 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "outer ligule"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part that is a rim or fringe of tissue on the abaxial (outer) side of a leaf at the junction of sheath and blade, opposite the ligule, as in bamboos and some other grasses."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:outer_ligule (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real grass/bamboo structure without a class. It cannot be is_a ligule (PO_0020105) because PO defines the ligule as adaxial. Used by 2 floras. Worth proposing to PO upstream alongside ligule. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "contra-ligule"@en,
        "contraligule"@en,
        "external ligule"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025034 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986090 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mesochile"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part that is the middle portion of a tripartite orchid labellum, between the hypochile and the epichile."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:mesochile (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: FLOPO already has hypochile (FLOPO_0986030) and epichile (FLOPO_0986029); the middle segment is missing. Propose upstream to PO together with them. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "mesochilium"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0980978 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986091 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "seed wing"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A thin, flat, membranous outgrowth of a seed that aids wind dispersal, formed from the seed coat or, in conifers, from tissue of the ovuliferous scale."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:seed_wing (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure (Bignoniaceae, Meliaceae, Pinaceae, Dioscorea) with no PO class. 'wing' alone was rejected as generic, but here the organ is given. The EQ 'seed winged' already exists for the quality. Part of seed, not testa, because the conifer wing comes from the cone scale. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "wing of seed"@en,
        "aile de la graine"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009010 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986092 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lignotuber"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A woody swelling at the base of the stem, at or below the ground, that holds dormant buds and food reserves from which the plant resprouts after fire or cutting."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:lignotuber (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Presence or absence is a diagnostic character in several floras (Arctostaphylos, Eucalyptus); there is no PO class. The French width/thickness examples may be trunk burls (abnormal wood swellings) and need checking. Propose upstream to PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "basal burl"@en,
        "root crown burl"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "burl"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009047 ],
        obo:PO_0025029 .

obo:FLOPO_0986093 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "calyx limb"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A collective organ part structure (PO:0025269) composed of the distal portions of the sepals (PO:0009031) of a fused calyx (PO:0025582), above the calyx tube (FLOPO:0986011); entire, truncate, toothed or lobed."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:calyx_limb (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Modelled on corolla limb (FLOPO:0986012) and the existing calyx tube and calyx lobe. 41 statements in 6 floras, mostly Rubiaceae. Propose to PO upstream together with corolla limb and the tubes. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "calyx limbs"@en,
        "limbe calicinal"@fr,
        "limbe du calice"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009060 ],
        obo:PO_0025269 .

obo:FLOPO_0986094 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "floral disc lobe"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is one of the divisions of a lobed floral disc (FLOPO:0986025)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:floral_disc_lobe (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Modelled on stigma lobe and corona lobe. The floral disc is not a phyllome, so phyllome lamina lobe cannot be used, and it is distinct from disc gland (FLOPO:0986045). The floral disc is a FLOPO class, so this is FLOPO-local, not proposed upstream until PO has the disc. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "disc lobe"@en,
        "disc lobes"@en,
        "disk lobe"@en,
        "lobe du disque"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0986025 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986095 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "vaginant lamina"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) of a non-vascular leaf (PO:0025075) that is the proximal, two-layered, sheathing portion of an equitant leaf, clasping the stem and the base of the next leaf, as in Fissidens."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:vaginant_lamina (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: 'vagrant' is an extraction error for 'vaginant' (the examples say 'vaginant laminae'). Do not add 'vagrant lamina' as a synonym; fix the normalization instead. Many moss floras describe Fissidens leaves this way. Propose upstream with the dorsal and apical laminae. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "sheathing lamina"@en,
        "vaginant laminae"@en,
        "vagrant lamina"@en,
        "vagrant laminae"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986096 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "involucre lobe"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is one of the free distal divisions of an involucre (PO:0009100) whose bracts are fused, as in the cyathium of Euphorbia."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:involucre_lobe (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Built like calyx lobe FLOPO_0986005 and corolla lobe FLOPO_0986006. Several floras need it: 38 statements here plus 32 under 'involucre tooth'. The qualities (triangular, ciliate, toothed, linear) fit. PO has no such class. Propose to PO together with calyx lobe and corolla lobe. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "involucral lobe"@en,
        "involucral lobes"@en,
        "involucral tooth"@en,
        "involucre tooth"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009100 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986097 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "stamen fascicle"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A collective plant organ structure (PO:0025007) that is part of an androecium (PO:0009061) and consists of a group of stamens (PO:0009029) whose filaments are connate at least at the base, as in Malvaceae, Hypericaceae and Myrtaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:stamen_fascicle (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure found in six floras. Counts of stamen fascicles ('5, 10 or 15 phalanges') are a standard character and cannot be expressed with stamen or androecium. PO has no class for it. Propose it to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "stamen bundle"@en,
        "stamen phalanx"@en,
        "staminal fascicle"@en,
        "staminal phalange"@en,
        "staminal-bundle"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "phalange"@en,
        "phalanges"@en,
        "phalanx"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009061 ],
        obo:PO_0025007 .

obo:FLOPO_0986098 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "guide cell"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A native plant cell (PO:0025606) that is one of a row of large, thin-walled cells in the costa of a non-vascular leaf (PO:0025075), seen in cross-section between the dorsal and ventral stereid (PO:0030045) bands."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:guide_cell (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A standard character of moss leaf cross-sections in several floras. PO has stereid PO:0030045 and stereome but no guide cell. Propose to PO (subset Bryophytes). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "deuter cells"@en,
        "guide cells"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "deuters"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0025606 .

obo:FLOPO_0986099 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "stomatal line"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure that is a single longitudinal row of stomatal complexes on the leaf epidermis, as on conifer needles; several adjacent lines may form a stomatal band."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:stomatal_line (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Conifer floras count lines, not stomata ('stomatal lines 4-7 along each surface'), so stomatal complex (PO_0002000) cannot carry the count. Propose to PO upstream along with stomatal band. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "line of stomata"@en,
        "stomatal lines"@en,
        "stomatal row"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0006016 ],
        obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986100 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "laminal cell"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A native plant cell (PO:0025606) that is part of the lamina of a non-vascular leaf (PO:0025075), outside the costa, the border and the alar region."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:laminal_cell (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: The most often described cells in moss floras, with their own states (quadrate, papillose, thick-walled). PO has alar cell but no general leaf-blade cell of the non-vascular leaf. Positions (proximal, medial, distal laminal cells) attach to this class via pattern 04. Propose to PO next to alar cell. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "lamina cells"@en,
        "laminal cells"@en,
        "leaf cells"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0025606 .

obo:FLOPO_0986101 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "spadix staminate zone"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure (PO:0009011) that is the portion of a spadix inflorescence (PO:0030120) bearing the staminate flowers (PO:0025600), as in Araceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:spadix_staminate_zone (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Shape and length (conic, cylindric, 4 mm long) belong to the zone as a whole, not to each staminate flower, so the part-of-qualified-whole pattern does not fit. Pairs with a pistillate zone class; FLOPO-local, could be proposed to PO with the spadix appendix. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "male part of spadix"@en,
        "male portion of spadix"@en,
        "male zone"@en,
        "male zone of spadix"@en,
        "spadix staminate part"@en,
        "staminate part of spadix"@en,
        "staminate zone"@en,
        "zone mâle"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030120 ],
        obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986102 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "rostellum lobe"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is one of the divisions of a lobed rostellum (FLOPO:0986017) of an orchid flower, such as the side lobes or arms of the rostellum in Habenaria."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:rostellum_lobe (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Modelled on stigma lobe, labellum lobe and corona lobe (2026-11-13). The bare word 'lobe' is rejected, and no generic lobe class exists for non-phyllome organs. 5 floras. Propose to PO together with rostellum, not on its own. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "rostellar lobe"@en,
        "rostellum arm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0986017 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986103 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "anther tube"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A collective organ part structure (PO:0025269) composed of the anthers (PO:0009066) of two or more stamens of an androecium (PO:0009061), connate laterally into a tube round the style, as in Asteraceae and Lobelioideae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:anther_tube (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: No class exists. Staminal tube (FLOPO_0986013) is fused filaments, and synandrium (FLOPO_0986014) is the whole androecium fused, anthers included. The anther tube is the pendant to staminal tube and is common in Asteraceae and Campanulaceae floras. Propose to PO upstream together with staminal tube. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "anther cylinder"@en,
        "syngenesious anthers"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009061 ],
        obo:PO_0025269 .

obo:FLOPO_0986104 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "perianth limb"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the expanded distal part of a fused perianth, above the perianth tube."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:perianth_limb (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: The sibling classes perianth tube (FLOPO_0986010) and corolla limb (FLOPO_0986012) already exist. Floras with a fused perianth (Aristolochiaceae, Nyctaginaceae, Thymelaeaceae, Iridaceae) describe the limb's colour and width. Keep in FLOPO with the tube; propose to PO together with the corolla and perianth tube and limb classes. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "limb of perianth"@en,
        "perigone limb"@en,
        "limbe du périgone"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025580 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986105 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "spadix pistillate zone"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure (PO:0009011) that is the portion of a spadix inflorescence (PO:0030120) bearing the pistillate flowers, together with the part of the spadix axis on which they are borne."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:spadix_pistillate_zone (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Araceae floras describe the shape and size of each spadix zone. The 2026-11-13 review noted 'No class for the zones of a spadix in PO' when it added spadix appendix (FLOPO_0986049). Propose upstream together with the staminate and sterile zones and the appendix. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "female flower zone"@en,
        "female zone"@en,
        "pistillate zone"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030120 ],
        obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986106 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "staminate zone of inflorescence"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure (PO:0009011) that is the portion of an inflorescence (PO:0009049), such as a spadix (PO:0030120) or a spike, that bears only staminate flowers, as in Araceae and Typha."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:staminate_zone_of_inflorescence (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real region measured in length and diameter (Typha spikes, aroid spadices); 'fertile/sterile staminate portion' are its kinds. No PO class for the zones of a spadix or spike; modelled on spadix appendix FLOPO_0986049. Pattern 12 (part of a qualified whole) cannot express a region of an axis defined by its flowers. Propose to PO with the other spadix zones. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "male portion"@en,
        "staminate portion"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009049 ],
        obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986107 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "emergence"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A multicellular plant structure that is an outgrowth formed from the epidermis together with underlying tissue, as distinct from a trichome, which arises from the epidermis alone."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:emergence (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real, well-defined structure ('petiole and rachis densely covered with emergences', needle-like, digitate). It fits neither trichome (non-sclerified epidermal outgrowth) nor prickle (PO: sclerified portion of epidermis). Propose to PO upstream as the parent of prickle. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "emergences"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986108 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hastula"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) of a vascular leaf (PO:0009025) that is a flap, crest or ridge of tissue at the junction of the petiole (PO:0020038) and the leaf lamina (PO:0020039), on the adaxial or abaxial side, as in palmate and costapalmate leaves of Arecaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:hastula (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A distinct palm structure described with its own shape, margin and texture in 5 floras; PO has no class. Should be proposed to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "abaxial hastula"@en,
        "adaxial hastula"@en,
        "hastulae"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009025 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986109 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "aerophore"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) of a fern leaf (PO:0009025) that is a pale, often swollen or linear outgrowth or line of aerating tissue at the base of a pinna or on the stipe, serving for gas exchange, as in Thelypteridaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:aerophore (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real fern structure used diagnostically in several fern treatments; no PO class. Worth proposing to PO together with frond/pinna (FLOPO_0985026/0985027). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "aerophores"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "pneumathode"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009025 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986110 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "corolla throat"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the region of a fused corolla (PO:0025581) where the tube widens into the limb, including the opening of the tube."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:corolla_throat (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Widely used in sympetalous families (width, hairs, colour marks, campanulate throat). It is neither apex, base nor margin, so the region patterns cannot express it, and FLOPO has corolla limb (FLOPO_0986012) but no throat. A bare 'throat' is often of the corolla but may be of a calyx or perianth tube; ground it by context. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "throat of corolla"@en,
        "gorge"@fr,
        "gorge de la corolle"@fr ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "throat"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025581 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986111 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "laesura"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure (PO:0009011) that is the linear scar or suture on the proximal face of a plant spore (PO:0025017), marking its contact with the other spores of the tetrad, along which the spore germinates; trilete (Y-shaped) or monolete (single line)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:laesura (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure used in fern and lycophyte floras ('proximal laesura more than 0.5 spore radius'). PO has no part of the spore wall. Propose to PO upstream with spore ornamentation. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "laesurae"@en,
        "tetrad scar"@en,
        "trilete mark"@en,
        "y-mark"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "commissure"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025017 ],
        obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986112 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "corpusculum"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A hard, dark, clip-like body secreted by the stigma head of the gynostegium that, together with two translator arms, joins the pollinia of adjacent anthers into a pollinarium and attaches it to a pollinator. Found in Apocynaceae subfamily Asclepiadoideae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:corpusculum (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A distinct structure described with its own size, shape and colour in milkweed treatments. It is not the orchid viscidium (FLOPO_0986032), which comes from the rostellum. FLOPO already has the related classes pollinium and gynostegium. Propose it to PO upstream together with pollinarium and translator arm. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "corpuscle"@en,
        "gland of the pollinarium"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "retinaculum"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0986051 ],
        obo:PO_0025496 .

obo:FLOPO_0986113 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pedicel scar"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the mark left on an inflorescence axis (PO:0020122) where a pedicel (PO:0030112) and its flower or fruit have been shed."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:pedicel_scar (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real, diagnostic structure (spacing and prominence of scars on old rachises, e.g. Annonaceae, palms) with no class. Propose to PO together with leaf scar. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "pedicel scars"@en,
        "cicatrice du pédicelle"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0020122 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986114 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "elater"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An elongated, sterile cell with spiral wall thickenings that lies among the spores in the capsule of a liverwort or hornwort. It twists as it dries and so helps to disperse the spores."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:elater (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Real and frequently described in bryophyte floras (colour, number of spiral bands, free or attached). PO has no class. The Equisetum 'elaters' are spore-wall bands rather than cells, so the definition is limited to bryophytes, or a sibling class could be added. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "elaters"@en,
        "spore elater"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025094 ],
        obo:PO_0009002 .

obo:FLOPO_0986115 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "faucal appendage"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An infolding or scale-like outgrowth of the corolla in the throat, opposite a corolla lobe, that partly closes the mouth of the tube, as in Boraginaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:faucal_appendage (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real, well-defined structure found in every Boraginaceae treatment, with its own shapes (quadrate, trapeziform, kidney-shaped, emarginate). No PO or FLOPO class covers it. Propose to PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "corolla appendage"@en,
        "faucal scale"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "fornices"@en,
        "fornix"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009059 ],
        obo:PO_0025496 .

obo:FLOPO_0986116 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "stipule scar"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the mark left on a shoot axis (PO:0025029) where a stipule (PO:0020041) has been shed."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:stipule_scar (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure and a common diagnostic character (Magnoliaceae, Moraceae, Rubiaceae), with its own qualities: annular, fringed, pubescent. It is a sibling of leaf scar (FLOPO_0986052). Propose it to PO upstream together with leaf scar. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "cicatrice stipulaire"@en,
        "stipular scar"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025029 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986117 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "stereid band"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A portion of ground tissue that consists of a longitudinal strand of stereids (PO:0030045) in the costa of a non-vascular leaf, seen in cross-section as a band of thick-walled cells abaxial or adaxial to the guide cells."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:stereid_band (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Standard character in moss floras (number and position of stereid bands in the costa). PO has the cell (stereid) and the costa but not the band. Propose to PO upstream (bryophyte anatomy). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "stereid bundle"@en,
        "stereid strand"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030072 ],
        obo:PO_0025059 .

obo:FLOPO_0986118 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pseudoperianth"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure (PO:0009011) of a liverwort gametophyte that is a sheath of gametophytic tissue growing up round an archegonium and the developing sporophyte after fertilization, as in Marchantia; distinct from the perianth of leafy liverworts, which is formed of fused leaves."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:pseudoperianth (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Bryophyte structure ('pseudoperianths conical, white or reddish, segments connate at apices'). It has nothing to do with the flowering-plant perianth (PO_0009058), so it must not map there. Propose to PO upstream with the bryophyte gametophore classes; part_of is left open because PO has no thallus class. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "pseudoperianths"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986119 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "asexual propagule"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant structure that becomes detached from the parent plant and grows into a new individual without sexual reproduction, such as a gemma, a brood body, a rhizoidal tuber or a deciduous branchlet."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:asexual_propagule (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Used mainly in moss floras ('specialized asexual reproduction by...', filamentous propagules). PO lists 'propagule' as a synonym of fruit, which is wrong here. PO gemma (PO_0025614) is limited to structures on a thallus. Propose to PO upstream, with gemma and bulbil (FLOPO_0986055) as children. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "brood body"@en,
        "vegetative propagule"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "propagule"@en,
        "propagulum"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0009011 .

obo:FLOPO_0986120 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "floret callus"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) of a spikelet floret (PO:0009082) that is the hardened, often pointed or hairy base of the floret, formed by the base of the lemma (PO:0009037) and often a segment of the spikelet rachilla (PO:0009080), by which the floret separates."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:floret_callus (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A standard grass character (FNA, FOC, Flora Zambesiaca), the bearer of callus hairs; PO has no class. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "anthecium callus"@en,
        "lemma callus"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "callus"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009082 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986121 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "chlorophyllose cell"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A plant cell (PO:0009002) of a non-vascular leaf (PO:0025075) of Sphagnum that is narrow, living and contains chloroplasts, forming a network between the large dead hyaline cells; its cross-sectional shape and exposure on the leaf faces are diagnostic."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:chlorophyllose_cell (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A rule to 'plant cell part of non-vascular leaf' would also cover the hyaline cells, so the diagnostic shapes (triangular, trapezoidal, exposed) would be wrong. PO already has moss leaf cell types (alar cell PO_0030057), so propose to PO upstream alongside the hyaline cell. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "chlorophyllose cells"@en,
        "chlorophyllous cell"@en,
        "chlorophyllous cells"@en,
        "green cells"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0009002 .

obo:FLOPO_0986122 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "clinandrium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the concave region at the apex of the orchid column, below and behind the anther, in which the anther rests. Its margin is often raised into a hood or wing."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:clinandrium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A named orchid structure with its own margin, indumentum and hood characters in 4 floras. Reading it as 'apex of gynostemium' would lose the hood and margin meaning. FLOPO already holds gynostemium, so propose both to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "anther bed"@en,
        "clinandrium-hood"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "androclinium"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0986015 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986123 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dorsal lamina"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the single-layered wing of a Fissidens leaf that lies on the abaxial side of the costa, opposite the vaginant lamina, and runs from the leaf apex towards the insertion."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:dorsal_lamina (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A key character in all Fissidens treatments (decurrent, rounded, narrowed at the base). It has siblings, the vaginant and apical laminae. It is genus-specific, so keep it in FLOPO for now and propose it to PO only together with its sibling classes. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "dorsal wing"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986124 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "endocarp condyle"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An intrusion of the endocarp into the locule of the fruit, around which the seed is curved, often hollow or perforate."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:endocarp_condyle (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: The key character of Menispermaceae fruits (present or absent, perforate, globose), used in five floras. Keep in FLOPO; it is family-specific, so it is a low priority for PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "condyle"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009086 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986125 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "endostome basal membrane"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the continuous, membranous lower part of the inner peristome (endostome) of a moss capsule, from which the endostome segments and cilia arise."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:endostome_basal_membrane (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A standard moss peristome character (height relative to the exostome, number of cell rows, smooth or papillose) across 4 floras. PO has peristome and peristome tooth but no endostome parts. Propose it to PO upstream together with endostome and its segments. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "basal membrane"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0030042 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986126 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "phyllid lamella"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is one of the longitudinal plates of photosynthetic cells, usually one cell thick, standing on the adaxial surface of a non-vascular leaf (PO:0025075), usually over the costa (PO:0030072), as in Polytrichaceae and some Pottiaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:phyllid_lamella (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: The marginal (apical) cells of the lamellae are key characters in moss floras; 'lamella' alone was rejected as generic, but the moss phyllid lamella is a definite structure with no PO class. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "costal lamella"@en,
        "leaf lamella"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986127 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "nodal diaphragm"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a transverse plate of tissue spanning the cavity of a hollow shoot axis at a stem node (PO:0020141), separating the hollow internodes, as in bamboos, Equisetum and many aquatic plants."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:nodal_diaphragm (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure that floras measure (thickness), and the thickness of the diaphragm is not the thickness of the node. PO has no class for it. Propose upstream to PO. Seen in one flora here, but standard in bamboo and Equisetum treatments. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "diaphragm"@en,
        "node diaphragm"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0020141 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986128 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "leaf vein axil"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is the region of the leaf lamina in the angle between the midvein and a secondary vein that branches from it, often bearing hairs or domatia."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:leaf_vein_axil (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Floras give qualities of this region itself (barbate, pubescent). PO axil (PO_0025224) is the angle between a leaf and the stem, so it does not fit. Dome-shaped or foveate pits are domatia (FLOPO_0986021) and should go there. Propose it to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "axil of lateral veins"@en,
        "vein axil"@en,
        "aisselle des nervures"@fr ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0020039 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986129 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cirrus"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A leaf rachis that extends beyond the uppermost leaflets as a long, leafless, whip-like and non-coiling extension armed with grapnel-like spines, by which climbing palms (rattans) attach to supports."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:cirrus (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A main palm character (cirrus present/absent, length, shape) found in three floras. The PO tendrils (leaf rachis tendril PO_0025366, leaf apex tendril PO_0025363) are defined as coiling, which a cirrus is not, so they would be wrong. The flagellum (a sterile inflorescence arising from the sheath) is a different organ: 'spiny climbing whips arising from...' is probably a flagellum and should not get this class. Propose to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "leaf whip"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "cirri"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009025 ],
        obo:PO_0020055 .

obo:FLOPO_0986130 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "syconium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An inflorescence (PO:0009049) in which numerous small flowers line the inner surface of a hollow, fleshy, urn-shaped receptacle that opens by a small apical pore (ostiole), as in Ficus; in fruit it develops into a multiple fruit (the fig)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:syconium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure that every flora treating Ficus uses ('syconia 1-3 in leaf axils'). PO has no class: the term only appears as a broadMatch to fruit, which misses the flowering stage. A proposal key FLOPO_LOCAL:syconium with evidence EVID:NYBG_SYCONIUM already exists but has no FLOPO id. Propose upstream to PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "syconia"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "fig"@en,
        "hypanthodium"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PO_0009049 .

obo:FLOPO_0986131 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "anther theca appendage"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a spur-, tail- or tooth-like outgrowth at the base or apex of an anther theca (PO:0009069), as in many Acanthaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:anther_theca_appendage (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure and a key character in Acanthaceae (Justicia and relatives) across tropical floras. Its shape and presence are recorded. PO has no class, and the generic 'appendage' was rejected. Propose upstream to PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "anther spur"@en,
        "basal appendage of theca"@en,
        "theca appendage"@en,
        "thecal appendage"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009069 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986132 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "carpopodium"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part at the base of a cypsela formed by a distinct ring or pad of differentiated, often sclerified cells, by which the fruit is attached to the receptacle and from which it separates."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:carpopodium (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A standard Asteraceae fruit character (present, shape, symmetry, colour) used by several floras. It has no PO class, and fruit columella or gynophore (PO_0004540, PO_0006330, PO lists 'carpophore') are different organs. Propose to PO upstream together with cypsela. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "basal callus"@en,
        "carpopodia"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0986053 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986133 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "floral spur"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) of a flower (PO:0009046) that is a hollow, tubular or sac-like extension of a petal, sepal, labellum or corolla, often containing nectar."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:floral_spur (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure in many floras (Orchidaceae, Aquilegia, Viola, Balsaminaceae, Linaria). It has no PO class: PO 'spur' is a synonym of short shoot PO_0004701, so 'spur' is grounded wrongly today. Should be proposed to PO upstream. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "nectar spur"@en,
        "éperon"@fr ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "calcar"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009046 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986134 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "velum"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a thin membranous fold of the adaxial base of a sporophyll (PO:0009026) partly or wholly covering the sporangium (PO:0025094), as in Isoetes."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:velum (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A standard diagnostic character in Isoetes ('velum complete', 'velum absent'). 'Shiny black and reticulate' is probably a misparse of the next statement (the spores). Keep it FLOPO-local first; it can be proposed to PO with the fern and lycophyte terms (indusium). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Isoetes velum"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009026 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986135 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "teniola"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A portion of plant tissue of a non-vascular leaf of Calymperaceae mosses forming a longitudinal band of elongate, thick-walled, often hyaline cells within the leaf lamina, between the costa and the margin."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:teniola (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real, named moss leaf structure (present/absent, conspicuous, interrupted) used for Syrrhopodon/Calymperes in three floras. It is not the border or the costa (PO_0030072). Propose to PO upstream with the moss leaf terms. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "taeniola"@en,
        "taeniolae"@en,
        "teniolae"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025075 ],
        obo:PO_0009007 .

obo:FLOPO_0986136 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "tegula"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a stalk of an orchid pollinarium derived from the epidermis of the rostellum (FLOPO:0986017), connecting the pollinia (FLOPO:0986016) to the viscidium (FLOPO:0986032)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:tegula (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: An orchid pollinarium part with no class. Siblings viscidium and caudicle are already FLOPO-local. Do not map 'tegula stipe' to the PO stalk rule (stipe -> stalk), which is about fern, gynoecium and fruit stipes. Propose to PO with the orchid batch. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "stipe of pollinarium"@en,
        "tegular stipe"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:FLOPO_0986017 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986137 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "anther wing"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a stiff, membranous lateral flange of an anther (PO:0009066); adjacent wings form the guide rails that lead the pollinator to the corpusculum, as in Asclepiadoideae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:anther_wing (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A standard character in Apocynaceae-Asclepiadoideae (shape 'right-triangular', 'closed', length). The generic 'wing' cannot carry it. Propose to PO with the gynostegium (PO issue 6). Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "anther flange"@en,
        "guide rail wing"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009066 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986138 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "false vein"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a vein-like strand of elongate, often thick-walled cells in a phyllome lamina (PO:0025396), not connected to the vascular system and without vascular tissue, as in many Hymenophyllaceae and some Pteridaceae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:false_vein (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: A real structure used by 3 floras (29 statements: present, absent, long, counted). It is not a leaf lamina vein (PO_0020138), which is vascular. PO has no class for it, so propose it to PO. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "false veinlet"@en,
        "fausse nervure"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "pseudovein"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0025396 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

obo:FLOPO_0986139 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "fruit beak"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cardinal organ part (PO:0025001) that is a narrowed, prolonged distal portion of a fruit (PO:0009001), often derived from the persistent style or the upper part of the ovary, as in the cypselas of Lactuceae, Cyperaceae achenes and Brassicaceae siliques."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Provisional FLOPO bearer; PO submission pending. Curator-approved FLOPO-local anatomy support class FLOPO_LOCAL:fruit_beak (Robert Hoehndorf, 2026-09-18; curation/flopo_anatomy_support_classes_20260918.tsv). PO check: Floras give the beak its own length, hairs and shape (beak 7-9 mm long, strigose), so it is a distinct part, not just an apex region. Other floras use it too (Asteraceae, Brassicaceae, Cyperaceae, Geraniaceae). 'Achene beak' is then fruit beak part_of achene fruit (PO_0030107). PO has no class for it, so propose it to PO. The bare word 'beak' stays rejected. Replace with the PO identifier via IAO:0100001 once assigned. No PO identifier is minted locally."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "achene beak"@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "beak"@en,
        "bec"@en,
        "rostrum"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty obo:BFO_0000050 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom obo:PO_0009001 ],
        obo:PO_0025001 .

